  "verificationNotes": "OAuth is the default. The hosted protected-resource metadata delegates to api.resend.com; CIMD supplies one durable public client identity and no secret. The requested emails:send scope intentionally permits only the documentation/source-backed send-email candidate and excludes API-key, domain, broadcast, contact, and admin tools. Official token examples contain no account/team identity and no identity endpoint is documented, so identity remains explicit opaque staged data pending authorized live verification. The supernala.com public origin is an undeployed staging assumption; render plugins/remotes/resend-cimd.json.template with the real approved PUBLIC_ORIGIN and update this declaration before review. The exact /v1/plugins/oauth/callback route and CIMD document must be deployed before consent. Live consent, hosted tools/list equality, team binding, privacy review, and production acceptance remain unverified."
